  "solution": {
    "text": "The electrovalent bond is favoured with a metal having low ionization energy and non-metal with high electron affinity.<br />The amount of energy released when one mole of an ionic compound is formed is called lattice energy. Higher the lattice energy more the stability of the ionic compound.&nbsp;",
